<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Eersteling reports half yr attr loss.</title>
<headline>Eersteling reports half yr attr loss.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-09-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Half year ended June 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>Revenue from gold</p>
<p>    and silver		  1.62     vs	13.65</p>
<p>    Working costs	     1.96     vs	17.04</p>
<p>    Working loss		0.34     vs	 3.39</p>
<p>    Net loss before tax     0.67     vs	 4.83</p>
<p>    Tax			    -	 vs	  -</p>
<p>    Attributable loss	 0.67     vs	 4.83</p>
<p>    Loss per share (cts)	 4     vs	   31</p>
<p>Full name: Eersteling Gold Mining Co Ltd (gold)</p>
<p>NOTE - The company said management had recognised that there was still a shortage of developed ore reserves which would introduce needed flexibility into the operation. It had therefore critically examined the current operation and decided to reduce the scale to allow sufficient time to develop reserves for a sustainable operation. But it would consider the possibility of temporarily suspending operations if the mine continued to run with a substantial negative cash flow.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
